--- body ---
## Context

Child of 1655. Run the screening over the whole not-yet-labelled pool, same rule
and same prompts as 1530: stage 1 Qwen on padme (or Haiku), stage 2 Opus on
"icf", "incertaine" and "proche" (decision of 30 September 2026: only "hors
sujet" leaves at stage 1; `config/rel_screen.yaml`), Fable audit of a sample of
stage 2.
Incremental: deliveries arriving after the first pass are screened by the same
command.

Stage 1 as of 2026-10-01 (author decision): local Qwen on padme for the pool
input of 2026-10-01 (run `2026-10-01-pool-stage1`), then local Gemma 4 if the
running benchmark passes; plus design B through OpenRouter for the leftovers
no local run takes (t1810-repec-local, t1790-sud-playwright, works re-keyed by
those merges; run `2026-10-01-designB-stage1`, PR 1659). Design B records two
stage-1 rows per work (Gemma 4 26B-A4B and Jev D1) and drops a work only when
both say "out" with Jev's P(out) >= 0.95 (`stage1_joint` in
`config/rel_screen.yaml`).
Precedence, recall first: a work carrying several stage-1 verdicts (a
re-keyed work screened by Qwen under its old key and by design B, a
re-screen) leaves at stage 1 only when every verdict is out; a design-B pair
is one verdict. 616 t1652+t1810 works are in that case: Qwen screens them
under their old `title:` keys, which the rebuilt pool no longer carries, so
those Qwen labels will show as not-in-pool residue in the view; importing
either Qwen run against the current pool needs `--allow-input-drift`.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Stage 1 on all unlabelled works of the pool, machine and run recorded
- [ ] Stage 2 on the stage-1 "icf", "incertaine" and "proche"
- [ ] Fable audit of a stage-2 sample, agreement measured
- [ ] REL view counts published from the table, with the run identifier
